From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:17:16 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] doze-rest

While the lid is shut or POWER has dozed the game, the device loop
draws two dark frames and then stops stepping, drawing and presenting.
It sleeps 50 ms per turn and still reads input, runs the timers, and
powers off or restarts on time, so waking costs at most one 50 ms poll.
A shutdown or a link keeps drawing. It logs when it starts resting and,
on waking, how long it rested, the presents per second and the CPU time
spent. From marghost/slot_modded b1f9e24, adapted from
suprsomething/slot.advance bf810b6 (both GPL-3.0),
https://github.com/marghost/slot_modded/commit/b1f9e24
https://github.com/suprsomething/slot.advance/commit/bf810b6
---
